  "question": {
    "text": "Let the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>108</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be such that it neither intersects nor touches the co-ordinate axes. If the point of intersection of the lines, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> lies inside the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then:",
